        "entry_h9Chri": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "full_width_enable": false,
            "title": "What do I do if my boundary wire is damaged?",
            "text": "<p>If the boundary wire becomes damaged for any reason, it is quite simple to repair using connectors supplied with the mower. Extra wire can be spliced into the boundary to extend or repair it. Insert the ends to be connected into any two of the holes in the connector and clamp it shut with grips or pliers. The connector is filled with water-repellent grease and is waterproof.</p>",
            "button_1_style": "white",
            "button_1_text": "",
