        "entry_yhk3EA": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "full_width_enable": false,
            "title": "What happens if there are obstacles on the lawn?",
            "text": "<p>The L12 is equipped with a bump sensor, meaning that if the mower bumps into a large, unmoving object, it will stop, reverse and continue in a different direction. However, it is recommended to remove or cordon off (using the boundary wire) sloping stones, trees with fragile bark, angled tree supports, exposed tree roots, shrubs and ponds<br/>to prevent damage to both the mower and the object.<br/><br/>Smaller objects such as children’s toys, pet toys, tools, sticks and small stones should be removed from the lawn as they pose a risk of damaging the mower.</p>",
            "button_1_style": "white",
            "button_1_text": "",
            "button_1_url": "",
            "button_2_style": "white",
            "button_2_text": "",
            "button_2_url": "",
