        "entry_iiEhDU": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "full_width_enable": false,
            "title": "I have multiple lawns; do I need two mowers?",
            "text": "<p>If you have two lawns which are connected by a corridor or path which wider than 1m and all on the same level, the L12 can navigate this as part of normal operation. We would not recommend that you attempt to allow the L12 to navigate a corridor of gravel, as this may damage the cutting mechanism.<br/><br/>If you have multiple lawns separated on different levels or separated by obstacles which would prevent the L12 from gaining access (such as a fence), the L12 will need to be moved manually to the secondary lawn. In order to do this, the boundary wire is set up as normal around the main lawn, and the secondary lawn is wired up as an island.<br/>For more details on how to set up the L12 to mow secondary lawns, please refer to the instruction manual.<br/></p>",
            "button_1_style": "white",
            "button_1_text": "",
            "button_1_url": "",
            "button_2_style": "white",
            "button_2_text": "",
            "button_2_url": "",
